WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.414 --> 00:00:01.725
- [Man] Do you think that

00:00:01.725 --> 00:00:05.034
the idea of hustle culture

00:00:05.034 --> 00:00:08.116
is becoming

00:00:10.736 --> 00:00:12.096
cliché?

00:00:13.586 --> 00:00:15.315
The thing about your hustle is

00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:17.658
it's hustle with 
tons of substance.

00:00:17.658 --> 00:00:19.030
- [Gary] Right.
- [Man] But I feel like there's a

00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:20.818
lot of kids who are 
just hustling to hustle.

00:00:22.868 --> 00:00:25.403
- [Gary] I think a lot of kids
are saying they're hustling

00:00:25.403 --> 00:00:27.281
to hustle. You know what I mean?

00:00:27.281 --> 00:00:29.658
- [Man] That's what I'm getting at.
- [Gary] Yeah.

00:00:29.658 --> 00:00:32.811
And by the way, by the way,
I'm just doing it to help the

00:00:32.811 --> 00:00:34.379
people that are actually 
trying to do it,

00:00:34.379 --> 00:00:36.314
realize how much work it is.

00:00:36.314 --> 00:00:38.001
I actually hope somebody 
else comes out with

00:00:38.001 --> 00:00:41.751
The Daily Z and shows 
unbelievable work-life balance.

00:00:41.751 --> 00:00:45.330
- [Man] Right. Right.
- [Gary] Just shows her or his

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:47.750
seven hour days but just 
enormous amounts of happiness

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:49.844
with family and bowling 
and learning new,

00:00:49.844 --> 00:00:51.884
"I'm going to learn how 
to knit this week."

00:00:51.884 --> 00:00:56.467
I don't want to convince 
anybody to do what I do,

00:00:56.467 --> 00:00:59.945
I just want to clarify 
to everybody that--

00:00:59.945 --> 00:01:03.068
- [Man] When you say hustle
this is what you mean.

00:01:03.068 --> 00:01:04.849
- [Gary] Look it takes 
a lot of work.

00:01:04.849 --> 00:01:06.757
You know the other thing 
that's helped a lot of people

00:01:06.757 --> 00:01:08.845
is people are like,
"Whoa, you're already

00:01:08.845 --> 00:01:12.699
"more successful than I am,
and I'm working like half

00:01:12.699 --> 00:01:15.842
"as much as you and 
I thought I was working more

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:18.596
"than you 'cause I thought you 
were kind of saying it but

00:01:18.596 --> 00:01:20.779
"then reaping the 
benefits of the riches.

00:01:20.779 --> 00:01:23.911
"If you're still doing that,"
so it's a context point.

00:01:23.911 --> 00:01:27.063
It's come up because of my 
last 24 hours on Snap I think

00:01:27.063 --> 00:01:30.760
not really. 
- [Man] Okay.

00:01:30.760 --> 00:01:32.210
- [Woman] It's interesting.

00:01:32.210 --> 00:01:35.749
- Once, like four times a year,
I'll collapse and go to sleep

00:01:35.749 --> 00:01:40.520
at 7 P.M. and I'll need a hard 
core like 15 hour sleep but

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:43.124
and I started taking care of 
my health about 2 years ago,

00:01:43.124 --> 00:01:47.167
18 months ago and I don't think 
I've picked up any more energy

00:01:47.167 --> 00:01:50.344
when I was 25 pounds heavier 
and eating like shit and

00:01:50.344 --> 00:01:54.030
not exercising. I just have so
much natural adrenaline.

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:55.750
I showed up to somebody's 
podcast yesterday

00:01:55.750 --> 00:01:57.280
and he was Facebook Live-ing

00:01:57.280 --> 00:01:58.911
and I went back and 
read all the comments

00:01:58.911 --> 00:02:00.248
last night at midnight

00:02:00.248 --> 00:02:01.968
'cause I don't get tired,

00:02:01.968 --> 00:02:04.968
and literally everybody's like, 
"This guy's on fucking drugs."

00:02:04.968 --> 00:02:06.247
Which is really interesting

00:02:06.247 --> 00:02:07.308
and they meant it 'cause

00:02:07.308 --> 00:02:08.563
they didn't know who I was.

00:02:08.563 --> 00:02:09.937
They're like, "Why do all these
guys have to take drugs?"

00:02:09.937 --> 00:02:12.447
And I was like "Fuck, I've 
never even tried a cigarette."

00:02:12.447 --> 00:02:14.603
"I've never done 
anything in my life."

00:02:14.603 --> 00:02:16.945
I've been left out from 
all that good shit

00:02:16.945 --> 00:02:20.408
and people still think it 
'cause it's just natural DNA.

00:02:20.408 --> 00:02:22.502
I truly think it's the 
same way as being pretty

00:02:22.502 --> 00:02:26.034
or 6-foot-5 it's just 
something you were given.

00:02:27.024 --> 00:02:28.498
I like it. I'm glad.

00:02:28.498 --> 00:02:30.517
I like that I,
I truly, truly,

00:02:30.517 --> 00:02:32.507
I really believe what 
I'm about to say and

00:02:32.507 --> 00:02:33.976
this is hyperbolized 
to the moon,

00:02:33.976 --> 00:02:36.104
I truly think I'm the hardest 
working person on earth.

00:02:36.104 --> 00:02:37.720
I truly believe that.

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:39.169
I just work 18 hours 
a day everyday.

00:02:39.169 --> 00:02:40.450
Like I just do.

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:42.061
- [Woman] Alright.
- [Gary] Cool.

00:02:42.061 --> 00:02:43.278
Awesome.
- [Man] Gary Vaynerchuk.

00:02:43.278 --> 00:02:44.749
Thanks guys.

00:02:44.749 --> 00:02:47.126
(applause)

00:02:47.126 --> 00:02:50.094
(light piano music)

